pve-bcachefs (0.0.6) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Take over the copy_volume virtual-xattr filter from
    pct-move-volume-snapshots. bcachefs reports its per-inode IO options
    through listxattr in two namespaces - bcachefs.*, the options set on an
    inode, and bcachefs_effective.*, the options in force after inheritance,
    which appear on every inode below a directory that sets any. Both are
    accepted by setxattr on bcachefs and rejected with EOPNOTSUPP everywhere
    else, so rsync -X aborts with exit 23 after copying everything and moving
    a container off bcachefs fails. Both namespaces are now filtered:
    bcachefs.* because it describes policy belonging to the source filesystem,
    bcachefs_effective.* because copying derived values pins what was
    inherited as an explicit per-inode setting on every file.
  * The patch was never a move-volume concern: it is needed with stock,
    unpatched pve-container, and it fixes nothing for any filesystem other than
    bcachefs. It belongs with the plugin for the filesystem whose xattrs it
    names, by the same rule that sent the snapshot-mount fix out to
    pve-lxc-snapshot-mount because that one repaired btrfs too.
  * patch-pve-container.pl now carries a series rather than a single change,
    applying and reverting each independently, and adopts the filter if an
    older pct-move-volume-snapshots already applied it.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:30:00 +0200

